{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": "Every file EchoForge is allowed to download, pinned to an immutable revision with a verified size and SHA-256. Nothing outside this file may be fetched. The runtime.* entries are the complete Windows / CPython 3.12 dependency closure for faster-whisper, resolved by uv from worker/requirements-production.in and regenerated by scripts/lock-worker-runtime.ps1; every one of them was downloaded and hashed locally, and the script refuses to write anything at all if a single digest, wheel, or licence is missing. The model entries are hand-pinned. Each digest was checked against the publisher's own index, and every entry except the 1.6 GB model weight file was additionally downloaded and hashed locally. faster-whisper's convenience alias 'large-v3-turbo' resolves to mobiuslabsgmbh/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo, which the Hugging Face API now redirects to dropbox-dash/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo: the alias moved, exactly as the architecture plan warned it could. The resolved repository and commit are recorded here and the alias is never used at runtime. Silero VAD is deliberately absent as a separate entry because faster-whisper 1.2.1 ships it inside its own wheel as faster_whisper/assets/silero_vad_v6.onnx (1245151 bytes), so the wheel's digest already covers it. NVIDIA CUDA and cuDNN runtime libraries are deliberately absent: EchoForge uses a system-installed CUDA runtime when one is present and falls back to CPU INT8 when it is not, and redistributing NVIDIA binaries needs the release-time review scheduled for Phase 6. The python.cpython-* entry is the app-local interpreter itself: EchoForge ships CPython rather than requiring one on the machine, and it is pinned by the same rule as everything else. It carries profiles ['any'] because every real profile runs a Python worker; the deterministic placeholder profile needs nothing downloaded and still does.",
